	(text "MODE1=0, MODE2=1; ADR2=ADR1=0 -> I2C 0x4C (7 bit). SCK grounded.\nBCK -> PLL reference; use 64fs BCK and I2S 32-bit slots. Enable normal clock-error handling.\nP0 R13 SRCREF=BCK (0x10). P0 R61/R62 = channel digital volume; ramp together for master volume.\nOUTL -> woofer (TPA right bridge); OUTR -> tweeter (TPA left bridge).\nR2/R3 + C16/C19 retain 470R/2n7 C0G output filtering; amp input pads limit full-scale level.\nXSMT pulled low by R32 until GPIO18 releases mute. Keep volume muted throughout setup.\nVCOM grounded in default VREF mode. LDOO decoupled; unused GPIO3-6 are no-connects.\nClock loss automatically powers down DAC/line drivers. Valid but incorrect DSP data still needs limiting.\nAll grounds share GND; route analogue return to source, away from amplifier switching currents."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c8573a7f-3f74-4977-a37c-a6ecb79c069c")
	)
	(text "PCM5122 - I2C VOLUME / MCLK-LESS I2S"
